{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 56, :comments ["<b>And the famine was over all the face of the land.</b> These are the rich, and they are called 'the face of the land' because everyone turns to them. From this we learn that the famine began only with the rich. And it says:" "<b>All that was in them.</b> That is, all the storehouses that were in them — grain. And thus the Targum says: אוצריא די בהון עבורא — 'the storehouses that had grain in them.'" "<b>And he broke out for Egypt.</b> He sold to them." "<b>And the famine intensified in the land of Egypt.</b> That they would eat and not be satisfied, in the manner of what is written (I Kings 18:2): ״והרעב חזק בשומרון״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:42.398892850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}